    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Campbells Auctioneers are delighted to present this attractive parcel of land to the open market, situated in the scenic townland of Crumlin, Ardara, Co. Donegal.\n\nExtending to approximately 0.61 acres, the property is offered for sale subject to planning permission and enjoys a peaceful rural setting while remaining conveniently located just a short drive from the vibrant heritage town of Ardara.\n\nRenowned as one of Ireland`s most picturesque towns, Ardara offers a wide range of amenities including shops, schools, cafés, restaurants, traditional pubs, and healthcare services. \n\nThe area is celebrated for its rich culture, stunning scenery, and outdoor lifestyle.\n\nNearby attractions include the spectacular Maghera Beach and Caves, the scenic Glengesh Pass, Loughros Point, and numerous beautiful beaches and coastal walks along Donegal`s Wild Atlantic Way, making this an ideal location for those seeking both tranquillity and accessibility.\n\nThis site presents an excellent opportunity for those looking to build a home in one of Donegal`s most sought-after locations, combining rural charm with easy access to local amenities and coastal attractions.\n\nFor further information, please contact Campbells Auctioneers.\n\nOur Ref: K1261"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Notice\nPlease note we have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate and photographs provided for guidance only."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Approximately 0.61 Acres </li><li> Convenient to Ardara Town </li><li> Close to beautiful beaches and coastal walks</li></ul>"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Negotiator",
        "SortOrder": 10,
        "Content": "Kenneth Campbell"
      }
    ],
